YeXuPDF NOTICE

YeXuPDF is derived from ClearPDF by Chethan616 under the MIT License.
Upstream: https://github.com/Chethan616/ClearPDF
The original ClearPDF copyright and attribution are retained in LICENSE, source comments,
and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The notes below describe components inherited from ClearPDF.

This project includes and adapts components from AndroidLiquidGlass by kyant0.
Source: https://github.com/Kyant0/AndroidLiquidGlass

AndroidLiquidGlass is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

This project depends on PdfBox-Android by Tom Roush, used for lossless PDF page
operations (merge, split, organize) and text extraction.
Source: https://github.com/TomRoush/PdfBox-Android
PdfBox-Android is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and is itself a
port of Apache PDFBox (https://pdfbox.apache.org/).

This project uses Google ML Kit (document scanner and on-device text recognition)
for the scanning and text-selection features only.

The offline build uses the U2NetP model from U-2-Net (Apache-2.0) through Microsoft
ONNX Runtime (MIT) for background removal. Inference is performed on the device.

The offline build packages a pinned LibreOfficeKit bundle derived from LibreOffice
(MPL-2.0 and accompanying third-party licences). See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The image editor adapts source code from ImageToolbox by T8RIN (Malik Mukhametzyanov),
Copyright (c) 2026, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Source: https://github.com/T8RIN/ImageToolbox
Adapted files keep their original Apache-2.0 header plus a "Modified by ClearPDF" line:
the Compose cropper (lib/cropper), gesture helpers (lib/gesture), image-scope helpers
(lib/image), the free-corners perspective cropper (lib/opencv-tools, with OpenCV replaced
by android.graphics.Matrix), and draw-engine geometry/paint/flood-fill code (feature/draw).
The image editor also depends on GPUImage for Android by CyberAgent (Apache-2.0).

ClearPDF remains licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
